{
 "what": "fidelity r1b, 2026-09-25: what PowerPoint (COM, one render) and PptxRender (app.engine.renderer) draw for every DrawingML line end, and for the space characters the extractor now keeps",
 "method": "A probe script emitted one deck through app.engine.emit on test-16x9: slides 1-5 one per line-end type, columns = stroke 0.75/1/1.5/2/3/4/6 px, rows = (w, len) sm/sm, med/med, lg/lg, sm/lg, lg/sm on a horizontal black line (tailEnd); rendered at 5120 px wide (4x). wPx = the head's largest vertical ink extent; lenPx = from the first column whose extent exceeds the shaft by 0.25 px to the last ink column (PowerPoint shortens the shaft under the head) or to the last such column (PptxRender, whose shaft runs on to the endpoint). The column threshold under-reads narrow ovals and diamonds (their ends are thinner than the shaft) and PowerPoint's open 'arrow' adds its stroke.",
